    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick mini.files\n\n### Description\n\nWith snacks.nvim recently introducing a input modules. I was wondering if there's a way to use that with mini.nvim's modules like MiniPick's `MiniPick.builtin.grep()` word input or MiniFiles confirmation message? Snacks.nvim input seems to work for things like vim.lsp.buf.rename.\r\n\r\nOr is that a different kind of input for the plugin. I'm not sure how this works, or if this already works, and maybe my config is wrong.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-12-12T14:52:47Z",
