            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nAll 'mini.nvim' modules prefer using `input()` Vimscript function (i.e. `vim.fn.input()`) to get input from the user because it is a blocking function which returns user's input as a string.\r\n\r\nThe 'folke/snacks.input' is an implementation of `vim.ui.input()` which is designed for asynchronous user input (by assuming later call to supplied callback). As documented design of `vim.ui.input()` is not suited for blocking call with returned value, it is relatively complicated to move 'mini.nvim' to use it *in all cases*. That's why I don't think this will happen any time soon (if at all).\r\n\r\nOne way to make `snacks.input` work with 'mini.nvim' input methods is to monkey-patch `vim.fn.input` to be a blocking call to `vim.ui.input()`. This is possible, but I'd not recommend this as it might cause unanticipated trouble.\r\n\r\nSo all in all, moving all 'mini.nvim' from `vim.fn.input()` to `vim.ui.input()` is certainly possible, but not worth a churn at this moment. I'd consider doing it if/when there is a dedicated `vim.ui.input()` in 'mini.nvim' (either synchronous or not). Closing as not planned (yet; in this form).\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\n> ... like MiniPick's `MiniPick.builtin.grep()` word input\r\n\r\nThis [indeed uses `vim.fn.input()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d084df4d6bf58abcc768b9bb326241ff0c502793/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1097-L1098), but can be made into a custom helper which uses `vim.ui.input()` for default `local_opts.pattern`:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal my_grep = function()\r\n  vim.ui.input({ prompt = 'Grep pattern: ' }, function(pattern) MiniPick.builtin.grep({ pattern = pattern }) end)\r\nend\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>fp', my_grep, { desc = 'Find pattern' })\r\n```\r\n\r\n> ... MiniFiles confirmation message\r\n\r\nThis one uses `vim.fn.confirm()` which will is slightly different than both `vim.fn.input()` and `vim.ui.input()`.",
